o the  assumed rules are you know we have our  information and our data and we don't  share it with anybody outside of the  intelligence community because you don't  have a need-to-know or you don't have  the architecture that we want you to  work with it on but we know that a lot  of that data can be used outside of our  architecture and with other people so  the data information doesn't have to be  kept secret not all of it just what  needs to be we can solve we can't solve  our problems alone so we need help to do  that and that was something we  determined we needed to come out and ask  for help with so the first thing we're  going to do is find the data inside nga  that we can use to invest in this way  and that's why we need more data savvy  or data experienced folks to come in and  help us work with that we're working on  that right now and that's what I would  call the hard but straightforward part  of the problem once we have that data we  would call that our capital in place we  can form our investment fund to invest  in this capital that might come in the  form of asking Co investors to chip in  their own data  so that we can work together on problems  so imagine nga in the Air Force or nga  and Google or nga and GrubHub working on  a large a problem together to co-invest  that's very similar to the approach  we've taken in the past  I mentioned GPS and Google Earth and  digital globe same kind of approach but  that was not with data that was about  technology this is now about data and  we're uniquely postured and uniquely  experienced to be able to do that so  we're looking for companies and  investors who have the skill and talent  and want to work with us that way we  realize that's not everybody where we  are the intelligence community we know  some people don't want any attachment  with that but we also know there are a  lot of people who want to serve their  government without putting on a uniform  or necessarily getting a government job  and this 